{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/981160-awakened-claimed","id":981160,"title":"Awakened Claimed","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-03T18:32:04-07:00","id":981160,"title":"Awakened Claimed","content":"Apologies if this has been addressed in a supplement, but what would happen if a spirit tried to Claim a Mage? I know Mages are probably well equipped to repel one, but what if it got past their defenses? And could a Mage use Spirit to deliberately initiate and manipulate the claiming process in their own body, ie binding a spirit to themselves and using it to change their body the way claiming does? Or, say, using Spirit to accelerate the Claiming process for another person to create an army of spirit-possessed superhuman minions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T19:32:47-07:00","id":981211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/981160-awakened-claimed#post981160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apologies if this has been addressed in a supplement, but what would happen if a spirit tried to Claim a Mage?</div> </div> </div> </div>If it succeeded you would have a Claimed mage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I know Mages are probably well equipped to repel one, but what if it got past their defenses? </div> </div> </div>No more than most supernaturals, I believe. Presumably this is a danger that those who deal in Goetia risk.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And could a Mage use Spirit to deliberately initiate and manipulate the claiming process in their own body, ie binding a spirit to themselves and using it to change their body the way claiming does? Or, say, using Spirit to accelerate the Claiming process for another person to create an army of spirit-possessed superhuman minions? </div> </div> </div>First there's a process of fusion, then once the Claim happens the mage would be out of commission. But making one use Claim on yourself or another would be relatively easy with Spirit. Or Death or Mind, if you wanted a ghost or Goetia to do it. You might be able to do something to safeguard your mind or soul while you were Claimed, if you wanted to observe. Having an army of Claimed would be possible but it would be tricky as a Claimed is no longer a spirit, so you would need something other than Spirit to control it.<br /> <br /> If you mean like letting them Claim just enough so you get the benefits, there's some Legacies that work like that but they aren't really Claimed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T22:28:51-07:00","id":981276,"title":"","content":"I see no reason why a Mage with Life &amp; Spirit couldn't do a controlled version of the Claimed, either replicating it with spells or a permanent version via Legacy.<br /> \u200bPersonally I like the idea of low Wisdom Mages binding spirits to people to create more than human minions. Really the Embodied Familiar is a lesser version in many ways. As for how to control them? You create your own court and rule them with the carrot and the stick, just like any other dominant spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T22:35:07-07:00","id":981278,"title":"","content":"Yeah. I started out wondering about claimed Mages, and then I ended up with the idea of an antagonist who forcibly turns people into Claimed to form an army of spirit-possessed minions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T07:06:36-07:00","id":982100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/981160-awakened-claimed?p=981276#post981276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see no reason why a Mage with Life &amp; Spirit couldn't do a controlled version of the Claimed, either replicating it with spells or a permanent version via Legacy.<br /> \u200bPersonally I like the idea of low Wisdom Mages binding spirits to people to create more than human minions. Really the Embodied Familiar is a lesser version in many ways. As for how to control them? You create your own court and rule them with the carrot and the stick, just like any other dominant spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh. This was <i>literally</i> one of my villains. Except the goal was more &quot;human empowerment&quot; and less personal rule. At least at first, of course.<br /> <hr /><br /> <b>Corollary</b>: Can a Mage with Mind and Spirit still mental resculpt spirits into new or copied personalities?<br /> <br /> Like: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Get Spirit and Subject</li> <li>Reformat the Spirit's mind/personality to be a copy of the subject.</li> <li>Force the Spirit to Claim the Subject.</li> <li>Subject's personality is (largely) unmodified, being a fusion of them and a copy of them.</li> </ol><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 10-05-2016, 10:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T07:19:52-07:00","id":982108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/981160-awakened-claimed?p=982100#post982100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Corollary</b>: Can a Mage with Mind and Spirit still mental resculpt spirits into new or copied personalities?<br /> <br /> Like:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Get Spirit and Subject</li> <li>Reformat the Spirit's mind/personality to be a copy of the subject.</li> <li>Force the Spirit to Claim the Subject.</li> <li>Subject's personality is (largely) unmodified, being a fusion of them and a copy of them.</li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so. Shape Spirit is pretty powerful and you would certainly be able to direct spirits or Claimed, but in the end you're redistributing Influences, not erasing them entirely. A Claimed still has an inherent need to do what it wants to get its resonant Essence. Even if you changed a spirit into a spirit of firefighting, and put it into a firefighter, you would have someone insanely obsessive about firefighting, as that need would replace all biological and psychological wants and desires. And of course, one can't fight fires without there being fires to fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T07:30:45-07:00","id":982113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/981160-awakened-claimed?p=982108#post982108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think so. Shape Spirit is pretty powerful and you would certainly be able to direct spirits or Claimed, but in the end you're redistributing Influences, not erasing them entirely. A Claimed still has an inherent need to do what it wants to get its resonant Essence. Even if you changed a spirit into a spirit of firefighting, and put it into a firefighter, you would have someone insanely obsessive about firefighting, as that need would replace all biological and psychological wants and desires. And of course, one can't fight fires without there being fires to fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know. That's the reason for the &quot;largely&quot; before unmodified. Just by virtue of what it now is, there would be the impetus for fulfilling the core Concept/Influence. But how is that different from acquiring an addiction or compulsive behavior? With everything else being the same, and the Claimed being part Flesh as well, I'm not sure <i>all</i> biological and psychological artifacts would be cast aside.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T07:55:57-07:00","id":982125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/981160-awakened-claimed?p=982113#post982113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know. That's the reason for the &quot;largely&quot; before unmodified. Just by virtue of what it now is, there would be the impetus for fulfilling the core Concept/Influence. But how is that different from acquiring an addiction or compulsive behavior?</div> </div> </div> </div>Addiction and compulsive behavior are based on memories and previous experiences with said addiction or behavior, but the mounts memories are not a part of the Claimed. They still exist, but it doesn't care about them outside of a resource. Plus then you get to the problem with Influence. It's not just about what the Claimed does. If you made a drug addict spirit Claim a drug addict, it would not sit alone in a room being addicted, it would seek to addict others.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With everything else being the same, and the Claimed being part Flesh as well, I'm not sure <i>all</i> biological and psychological artifacts would be cast aside. </div> </div> </div>With just Spirit as shown, there's a limit to how much you can Shape a spirit. But even if you pushed that aside, maybe with Spirit 6 or something, you still have a being that doesn't just exist the way humans do. If you made a spirit fully John, a copy of John in spirit form, it would shrivel up and die over time because there's no resonant Essence of John. Well, it would go dormant. You could stave that off by forcing said spirit to Claim John. But it's going to try to seek out John, make more John. It would use its Influence to make people John because simply being John is not enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-05-2016, 11:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T08:07:12-07:00","id":982128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/981160-awakened-claimed?p=981278#post981278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. I started out wondering about claimed Mages, and then I ended up with the idea of an antagonist who forcibly turns people into Claimed to form an army of spirit-possessed minions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are they a Claimed Mage that's creating other Claimed? Because that could be pretty cool. They would likely not need to use magic to control them either as the other Claimed would probably see them as their rightful leader depending on what kind of spirits make up the fusion.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T17:07:01-07:00","id":983016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/981160-awakened-claimed#post981160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apologies if this has been addressed in a supplement, but what would happen if a spirit tried to Claim a Mage? I know Mages are probably well equipped to repel one, but what if it got past their defenses? And could a Mage use Spirit to deliberately initiate and manipulate the claiming process in their own body, ie binding a spirit to themselves and using it to change their body the way claiming does? Or, say, using Spirit to accelerate the Claiming process for another person to create an army of spirit-possessed superhuman minions?</div> </div> </div> </div>I ran an occult game with a very different system and setting (using GURPS Path magic) which, like any good GURPS game, wasn't really about balance, and allowed characters to use the Spirits rules to have a friendly spirit possess them and become something akin to Claimed with greater exposure. Works fine, so long as you don't mind becoming a new person, essentially, with blended beliefs.<br /> <br /> If you allow this, keep in mind that you're allowing a player to have a fairly enormous boost in their capabilities. About the only balancing factor would be A) the vast majority of Werewolves would declare the biggest fucking <i>Siskur-da</i> and B) your character <i>must</i> play the character radically differently in accord with the union.<br /> <br /> Does make for excellent villains.<br /> In another game, a Werewolf one, one character deliberately caused someone else to be Claimed - not because they were trying to hurt them, but because they felt that they and the spirit were perfect for one another and the resulting person was a better whole. They were correct! And of course warned them not to act up, because they won't be there if they attract attention on their heads.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T10:05:47-07:00","id":983387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenorath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/981160-awakened-claimed?p=982128#post982128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are they a Claimed Mage that's creating other Claimed? Because that could be pretty cool. They would likely not need to use magic to control them either as the other Claimed would probably see them as their rightful leader depending on what kind of spirits make up the fusion.</div> </div> </div> </div> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Extract your Daemon as an incarnate (using Spirit) Goetia.</li> <li>Extract the rest of your Goetia and incarnate them.</li> <li>Have your Daemon-Goetia Claim you.</li> <li>Have your other Goetia Claim minions.</li> <li>...?</li> <li>Profit!</li> </ol><br /> <hr />Alternatively, have <i>all</i> your Goetia Hive-Claim you. Enjoy the existential question of who you are when you are a fusion of all mental facets of who you are, while enjoying a side of Dread Powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 10-07-2016, 01:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}